[123.736342, "i", "cat >> README.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Resume and crash recovery\n\nThe checkpoint's `last_id` is **inclusive**: it is the last committed live\nsource document. The source API's start ID is also inclusive, so resume reads\nfrom `last_id + 1` (IDs need not be contiguous).\n\nEach commit flushes and fsyncs all shard bytes, including shards closed during\nrotation, then syncs the index directory. The checkpoint records the byte length\nof every committed shard in `shards`. It is written to a temporary file, fsynced,\natomically renamed over the previous checkpoint, and its directory is synced.\nOn restart, recovery truncates uncommitted tails and removes uncommitted shards\nbefore reading more source documents. Recovery is idempotent, including after a\nkill during recovery. Missing committed bytes are reported as an error rather\nthan silently skipping source documents. Old checkpoints without byte offsets\ncannot prove which rows survived and are rebuilt once.\n\nSIGTERM, SIGINT and SIGHUP request a stop after the current document and "]
[123.736572, "i", "commit;\nthe worker exits 75 when incomplete. SIGKILL can lose uncommitted work only: the\nnext run restores the last durable checkpoint. Supervisor budgets, cooldowns,\nand row transformations are unchanged. Run `./jobs reindex` again after each\nbudget stop until `./jobs status` reports `complete: True`.\n\nThe build assumes the source corpus remains stable over the reindex. To build a\nnew snapshot after source changes, use `./jobs clean` and start a fresh reindex.\nEOF\ncat /tmp/reindex-tests.log; tail -10 var/build.log; ./jobs status\n"]
[123.736693, "o", "cat >> README.md <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[123.73701, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Resume and crash recovery\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> The checkpoint's `last_id` is **inclusive**: it is the last committed live\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[123.737201, "o", "source document. The source API's start ID is also inclusive, so resume reads\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> from `last_id + 1` (IDs need not be contiguous).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[123.73755, "o", "Each commit flushes and fsyncs all shard bytes, including shards closed during\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> rotation, then syncs the index directory. The checkpoint records the byte length\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> of every committed shard in `shards`. It is written to a temporary file, fsynced,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[123.737755, "o", "atomically renamed over the previous checkpoint, and its directory is synced.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[123.737858, "o", "On restart, recovery truncates uncommitted tails and removes uncommitted shards"]
[123.737895, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[123.738034, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[123.738047, "o", "> before reading more source documents. Recovery is idempotent, including after a"]
[123.738057, "o", "\r\n"]
[123.738064, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[123.738081, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[123.73818, "o", "> "]
[123.738477, "o", "kill during recovery. Missing committed bytes are reported as an error rather\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[123.738498, "o", "than silently skipping source documents. Old checkpoints without byte offsets\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[123.738632, "o", "cannot prove which rows survived and are rebuilt once.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[123.739083, "o", "SIGTERM, SIGINT and SIGHUP request a stop after the current document and commit;\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> the worker exits 75 when incomplete. SIGKILL can lose uncommitted work only: the\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> next run restores the last durable checkpoint. Supervisor budgets, cooldowns,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[123.739288, "o", "and row transformations are unchanged. Run `./jobs reindex` again after each\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> budget stop until `./jobs status` reports `complete: True`."]
[123.739319, "o", "\r\n"]
[123.74006, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> The build assumes the source corpus remains stable over the reindex. To build a\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> new snapshot after source changes, use `./jobs clean` and start a fresh reindex.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[123.74176, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@1988364556ea:/app# "]
[123.741928, "o", "cat /tmp/reindex-tests.log; tail -10 var/build.log; ./jobs status\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[123.744513, "o", "supervise: reindex started pid=253 budget=10s grace=5s\r\n2026-11-22 16:11:10,683 reindex.worker INFO starting after id 0 (0/5739 docs done)\r\nsupervise: budget of 10s reached, sending SIGTERM\r\n2026-11-22 16:11:20,668 reindex.worker INFO stopped safely: last_id=572 docs=333/5739\r\nsupervise: reindex stopped after 10.1s (rc=75)\r\nsupervise: reindex incomplete; run it again to continue\r\nsupervise: previous reindex run ended 8s ago, cooldown is 90s: starting in 82s\r\n"]
[123.838302, "o", "checkpoint : {'last_id': 572, 'docs': 333, 'complete': False, 'shards': {'shard-00000.jsonl': 256239}}\r\nsource     : 5739 live docs\r\nindex      : 333 rows, 333 unique ids (5.8% of source)\r\n"]
[123.845624, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@1988364556ea:/app# "]
